# Never commit a folder's corpus binding. It names a subject, and a pasted key
# would be a live read of that subject for anyone holding the repo.
.mcp.json

# Except THIS repo's own, at the root, which is the opposite thing: it is the
# connector the plugin SHIPS, and it is why installing the plugin now gives you
# the corpus tools with no command to run. It carries a public URL and no
# credential, because authorizing is the Connect flow rather than a header, so
# there is nothing here to leak. The rule above still covers a nested one.
!/.mcp.json

# Local Claude Code state
.claude/settings.local.json

# Secrets
.env
.env.*

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

node_modules/
*.log
